<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">National Action Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as PAN</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The National Action Party (PAN) is a conservative Mexican political party founded in 1939 by Manuel Gómez Morín, drawing on Catholic and business opposition to the ruling party. For decades a minor opposition, it won its first state governorship in 1989 and the presidency in 2000 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vicente-fox">Vicente Fox</a>, ending 71 years of PRI rule. Felipe Calderón held the presidency for it from 2006 to 2012.</p></div>
